{"task_id": "HumanEval/123", "solution": "def _is_odd(number):\n    \"\"\"Checks if a given number is odd.\"\"\"\n    return number % 2 != 0\ndef _calculate_next_collatz_term(current_term):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the next term based on Collatz rules.\"\"\"\n    if current_term % 2 == 0:\n        return current_term // 2\n    else:\n        return 3 * current_term + 1\ndef get_odd_collatz(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given a positive integer n, return a sorted list that has the odd numbers in collatz sequence.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 1:\n        return [1]\n\n    odd_numbers_list = []\n    current_term = n\n\n    # Generate Collatz sequence until 1 is reached.\n    while current_term != 1:\n        # Identify and collect odd numbers.\n        if _is_odd(current_term):\n            odd_numbers_list.append(current_term)\n        # Calculate the next term based on Collatz rules.\n        current_term = _calculate_next_collatz_term(current_term)\n\n    # After the loop, current_term is 1. Add 1 as it's always odd and the sequence terminates there.\n    odd_numbers_list.append(1)\n\n    # Sort the collected odd numbers in increasing order.\n    odd_numbers_list.sort()\n    return odd_numbers_list"}
